factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 7 problems
  reel_script says the minister 'கல்வித்துறை அமைச்சரிடம் பேசி நடவடிக்கை எடுப்பதாக உறுதியளித்தார்' merges two things: the article says he would urge the education minister to act on the teachers' petition, not that he personally promised action on it; and the article's direct wording is ambiguous/mixed with the general assurance.
  reel_script says 'அமைச்சர் உதவியாளரிடம் மாணவியின் விவரங்களை எழுதிக்கொள்ள உத்தரவிட்டார்' - the article says he asked the assistant to take the student's name, address and mobile number, which is accurate, but the reel omits the student's stated concern that her mother was unwell being connected to the assistant's note; minor, but the mother's illness is presented as a complaint to the minister rather than a plea for help ('அம்மாவை காப்பாத்துங்க').
  reel_script states 'அனைத்து தரப்பினரின் கோரிக்கைகளுக்கும் நடவடிக்கை எடுப்பதாக அமைச்சர் உறுதியளித்தார்' which overstates the article, where the minister said he would ask to take action on certain items and gave a general assurance after listening to requests.
  The reel_script and caption omit the important fact that the minister only assured action on requests, and omit that the teachers' and student's requests were heard standing; also omits that the minister asked the municipal commissioner about the missing playground and whether an alternative site could be bought, which is only partially reflected.
  The caption's 'நடவடிக்கை' line says 'பள்ளி வசதிகள் மற்றும் மக்கள் கோரிக்கைகள் குறித்து ஆய்வு மற்றும் உறுதி' and the 'மக்கள் கவனத்திற்கு' line says action will be taken on 'ஆசிரியர் நியமனம்', which the article does not state about teacher recruitment as a promised action.
  slides_spec slide 'மக்கள் கோரிக்கை' says 'ஆசிரியர்கள், மாணவி உடல்நலம் குறித்து கேட்டனர்', which is a mixed and unclear sentence: the teachers' concern was about the recruitment-exam petition, not health, and the sentence merges two different requesters into one line.
  slides_spec and reel mention 'நவம்பர் 13ம் தேதி' for the event; the article gives the date as 'இன்று (நவ.,13)' so this matches, but the caption date line uses 2026 which is only the posting date, acceptable.
